{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 797 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D4"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the remifentanil hydrochloride shortage on 2022-06-28 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E24", "D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage listing includes Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc., and Mylan Institutional, a Viatris Company.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E22", "E23"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale sites use product labeled by Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. with NDC 00143939210.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That NDC is linked to two registered plants: Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1925262) and Navinta LLC (FEI 3004375014).",
      "cites": ["E14", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1064827 at Hospira, Inc. ended 2018-08-15 and was classified OAI; the classification letter is dated 2020-04-22, 797 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E10", "D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 971010 at Navinta LLC ended 2016-05-16 and was classified OAI; the classification letter is dated 2018-04-20, 1530 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E16", "D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based transfer option is to move 16 vials of 2 mg/2 mL, 5 mL from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside, which would give Corvale Lakeside 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    }
  ]
}
